The arithmetic shared by `hash_word` and `hash_bytes`:

- `hash_secret`: wyhash's four odd constants with balanced bits, mixed into every round.
- `hash_multiply(left, right)`: the full 128-bit product in place, low half into left, high half
  into right (`unsigned __int128`, one `mul` on x86-64).
- `hash_mix(left, right)`: that product folded to 64 bits, low ^ high: the step that makes every
  output bit depend on every input bit.

All three are always inlined; a call would cost more than the multiply.
